  "decision": {
    "answer": "SUPPORTS",
    "explanation": "The evidence from pmid-24335962 supports the claim that AKT3 overexpression is predictive of sensitivity/response to the Pan-AKT Kinase Inhibitor GSK690693 in Triple-receptor Negative Breast Cancer (TNBC). The source text explicitly states that AKT3 is upregulated in TNBC cell lines and that depletion of AKT3 sensitizes these cells to GSK690693, implying that therapeutic targeting of AKT3 is a viable treatment option for TNBCs. This aligns with the claim's disease, molecular profile, therapy, and significance.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-24335962",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 524,
        "quote": "AKT3 was found to be preferentially required for the proliferation and tumor growth of TNBC. It was found to be upregulated in a set of TNBC cell lines compared to other breast cancer types. Depletion of AKT3 in TNBC sensitizes cells to the pan-Akt inhibitor GSK690693. It was found that depletion of Akt3 potentially inhibits the growth of TNBC cell lines in three-dimensional (3D) spheroid cultures and in mouse xenograft models, which imply that therapeutic targeting of AKT3 may provide a new treatment option for TNBCs."
      }
